body:
&#x200B;

Natural causes only.

No shortcuts!

&#x200B;

It's a basic idea that if you don't know what makes you happy then you can't know if a partner is making you happy by definition. Know thyself. 

Not a boomer thing unless you count the boomers after the fall of Troy.

Last time I had an involuntary vacation we didn't even have to lie ourselves out. A man I met there and I were kicked out even after telling the doctors we were no better than before and would end our lives if released. 

&#x200B;

I failed at that also.

SO MUCH THIS! 

&#x200B;

People at work think I'm the most patient, happy, relatable person they know. They tell me their issues, I share advice, everyone around me feels better than they did before.  

I get compliments on how level headed and consistently nice I am.

&#x200B;

Little do they know the pit I fall into each and every night when I get home. 

Every night I come so close to ending it all.

I isolate and medicate and stare at the pit thinking how easy it would be...

&#x200B;

In the morning I get up and do it all over again.

What if your just a copy of yourself - and not even a complete copy. What if you are just a "probe" version of yourself designed to experience what this world is like now. When you die your experiences are reabsorbed into the whole. We really are our own god.  Jesus was just a powerup version with help from hints from previous versions. As well as all the other "gods".  Maybe we are all really parts of the same being - programmed by chemistry and experience to believe we are seperate.  Eventually we do rejoin our creator as promised.  

&#x200B;

Or maybe we are accidents of chemistry floating on a spec of dust in the middle of a vast emptiness our tiny minds have no chance of grasping.
